abstract: >-
  OCDocker integrates the stages of a virtual-screening campaign that are usually
  fragmented across independent tools -- molecular preparation, docking with multiple
  engines, automated pose selection, rescoring, descriptor extraction and machine-learning
  training -- into a single configurable, traceable workflow. It also implements OCScore,
  a consensus score that combines classical scoring functions with ligand and receptor
  descriptors, together with an ablation framework and SHAP-based shortcut-risk analysis
  for auditing what a learned score actually relies on.
